<title>ITALY: Italy's Perugia sees March CPI at +0.3 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Perugia sees March CPI at +0.3 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>PERUGIA, Italy 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Perugia said its March consumer price index rose 0.3 percent month-on-month and 2.2 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In February, Perugia's inflation rate was 0.3 and 2.2 percent respectively. The general index and housing and utility charges sector have been revised to take account of a court ruling last month that suspended electricity tariff reductions.</p>
<p>Perugia is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data Thursday and Friday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 1.26 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent of the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to February 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.3    (0.3R)   2.2  (2.2R)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.3   (-0.3)    0.7  (1.2)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.1    (0.2)    4.3  (4.5)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.5    (1.0R)   5.1  (4.6R)</p>
<p>    Furniture			  -0.1    (0.0)    0.4  (0.4)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0    (0.2)    3.6  (3.6)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.3    (0.6)    1.4  (2.9)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     2.2    (1.7)    7.0  (4.7)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0    (0.4)    5.6  (6.6)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0    (0.0)    0.3  (0.3)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.5    (0.9)   -0.1 (-0.3)</p>
<p>R = revised</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
